 "cleared_is_the_weakest_bar": "`cleared_own_floor` compares the point delta to the lane's recorded rho floor and nothing else. It is not a verdict: a verdict needs the Holm correction across that lane's family, and for anything gated after 2026-09-06 the co-primary contributor-AUC leg as well. It is published because the count of arms that reached even this bar is the honest way to describe the program's yield.",
 "reading": "48 arms have been adjudicated across 6 lanes, 39 of them scoreable against a recorded floor, and 0 reached that floor on the point estimate. At a nominal 5% per arm, pure noise alone would be expected to produce about 2.4 passes across 48 arms. Fewer arms cleared than noise alone would produce, which says the per-lane floors are, if anything, conservative, and that the program's run of nulls is a real result rather than a reporting artifact. Every lane's own Holm correction is correct and controls the error rate WITHIN that lane; nothing has ever controlled it across lanes, because until now nothing counted them. Read any survivor against this denominator.",
 "this_is_not_a_correction": "no program-wide Holm is applied and none should be. The arms were gated on different frames, pools and label definitions, so a retrospective joint family would imply a structure that never existed. The count makes the denominator visible; the reserved 2025 fold is what actually buys confirmation.",
 "reserved_fold": {
  "cohort": "2025 base year",
  "status": "not yet resolvable",
  "enters_at_run_year": 2028,
  "rule": "held out of every exploratory read so the confirmatory read has rows the exploration never touched. A survivor found and confirmed on the same rows is worth nothing.",
